 Corpolitarian regimes cannot control the justice system directly, so they employ coercive design and dark patterns to slowly redraw the boundaries of legality
  
 This video is firstly about the unwavering faith I have in humankind — and in this specific moment in history and secondly about how the quality of information we consume directly shapes the standards we're capable of holding, and how corpolitarian regimes actively erode that quality.
